    "submission": {
      "payload": {
        "approvalEvidenceComplete": true,
        "findings": [
          {
            "affectedPaths": [
              "packages/web/src/workers/triageWorker.js"
            ],
            "category": "maintainability",
            "claim": "Triage decision log records 'skipped'/'no labels to apply' even when a triage comment was posted, and omits auto_comment from its conditions/configUsed snapshot",
            "confidence": 0.8,
            "description": "The main triage decision log entry (triageWorker.js:332-346) computes decision and reason solely from labelsToApply ('skipped' / 'no labels to apply' when no labels matched or auto_label is false) and its configUsed snapshot only includes auto_label. After this change, the worker posts a marker-backed summary comment for every successfully triaged issue when auto_comment is enabled (L358-401), so for repos with auto_label:false or classifications with no matching labels, the decision log now routinely says the triage 'skipped' while a visible GitHub comment mutation was actually performed, and the audit snapshot never shows which auto_comment value governed it. This discrepancy pre-existed for the narrow needs_more_info/duplicate_hint subset, but the change broadens it to every such issue. Observability/audit-accuracy issue only; the managed-actions ledger still records the comment via propose/succeed.",
